Pymtheg patch 0010 (C-21, not upstream): a lifetime first in `dyn` bounds.

Accepts valid Rust: `dyn 'a + Display`, `dyn 'static + for<'a> FnMut(..)`.
A trait object's bounds may list the lifetime before the trait. Read as
`dynamic_type(trait: bounded_type(lifetime, trait))`, the shape upstream
PR #258 gives `impl 'a + Trait`. `dyn Trait + 'a` keeps its old tree.
Reference: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/types/trait-object.html
Upstream: no issue or pull request for `dyn`; PR #258 (merged) did `impl`:
https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-rust/pull/258 (fixing issue #234,
https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-rust/issues/234).

